.TH kannadi 1  "kannadi 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
kannadi \- Convert Kannada documents between legacy fonts and Unicode
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkannadi\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert Kannada documents between legacy fonts and Unicode.
.PP
to\-unicode reads text typed in Nudi, Baraha ANSI, Nudi B\-Akshara, Kan\-Eng, Akruti and Shree\-Lipi fonts in TXT, HTML, DOCX and PDF files. to\-nudi writes Unicode Kannada as Nudi glyph codes.
.PP
Each converted file gets a report next to it, FILE.report.tsv, when anything could not be converted cleanly or the result has likely typos.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
kannadi\-to\-unicode(1)
Convert documents in legacy Kannada fonts to Unicode
.TP
kannadi\-to\-nudi(1)
Convert Unicode Kannada documents to Nudi glyph codes
.TP
kannadi\-normalize(1)
Normalize Unicode Kannada text, following the Kannada text normalization profile
.TP
kannadi\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script to standard output
.TP
kannadi\-manpages(1)
Write the man pages to a folder
.SH EXTRA
Exit status:
  0  Success. Reports may still list problems and likely typos.
  1  \-\-strict was given and a file has a problem.
  2  Bad arguments, or a file that could not be read, converted or written.
     2 wins over 1 when both apply.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
